Ngurah Rai Airport to Uluwatu Transfer

Travelling from Ngurah Rai Airport to Uluwatu?

BaliWest Transport provides private airport transfers from Bali Airport directly to hotels, villas, resorts, surf camps, and accommodation throughout Uluwatu. Whether you are staying in Pecatu, Bingin, Padang Padang, Suluban, or Balangan, our airport transfer service offers a comfortable and hassle-free journey from arrival to destination.

A pre-booked airport transfer allows travellers to avoid taxi queues, price negotiations, and transportation uncertainty after landing in Bali.

How to Get from Ngurah Rai Airport to Uluwatu

There are several ways to travel from Bali Airport to Uluwatu, including taxis, ride-hailing services, scooter rentals, and private airport transfers.

For most visitors, a private airport transfer is the easiest and most convenient option because it includes airport pickup, luggage assistance, and direct transportation to your accommodation.

Transport Options Comparison
Transport Option	Best For	Luggage Friendly	Direct Transfer
Private Airport Transfer	Families, couples, groups	Yes	Yes
Airport Taxi	Flexible travel	Yes	Yes
Ride-Hailing Apps	Budget travellers	Moderate	Yes
Scooter Rental	Solo travellers	Limited	Yes

Visitors arriving with surfboards, multiple bags, children, or large groups often prefer private airport transfers for added comfort and convenience.

Distance from Bali Airport to Uluwatu

The distance from I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport to Uluwatu is approximately 18 to 25 kilometres depending on your final destination.

Uluwatu is a broad area that includes several popular locations such as:

Pecatu
Bingin
Padang Padang
Suluban
Balangan
Dreamland

The exact distance will vary depending on where your accommodation is located.

Travel Time from Bali Airport to Uluwatu

The journey from Bali Airport to Uluwatu typically takes between 35 and 70 minutes.

Travel time can vary based on:

Traffic conditions
Time of day
Weather conditions
Holiday periods
Destination within Uluwatu

Morning arrivals often experience faster journeys, while evening traffic can increase travel times, particularly around Jimbaran and major routes into the Bukit Peninsula.

Why Choose a Private Airport Transfer
Fixed Pricing

Know your transportation cost before you arrive in Bali.

Meet and Greet Service

Your driver will wait in the arrivals area and assist with luggage.

Flight Monitoring

Pickup times can be adjusted if your flight arrives later than scheduled.

Comfortable Vehicles

Travel in air-conditioned vehicles suitable for individuals, couples, families, and groups.

Direct Hotel or Villa Drop-Off

Enjoy door-to-door service without additional stops or transfers.

Areas We Cover in Uluwatu

BaliWest Transport provides airport transfers throughout the Uluwatu region.

Pecatu

Pecatu is home to luxury resorts, cliffside villas, golf courses, and some of Bali's most famous ocean views.

Bingin

Bingin is popular among surfers and travellers looking for boutique accommodation close to the beach.

Padang Padang

Known for its beautiful beach and surf breaks, Padang Padang attracts visitors from around the world.

Suluban

Suluban is one of Bali's most recognised surfing destinations and is located near Uluwatu Temple.

Balangan

Balangan offers a quieter atmosphere and is popular with visitors seeking a more relaxed beach experience.

Popular Attractions Near Uluwatu

Many travellers heading to Uluwatu stay close to some of Bali's most famous attractions.

Uluwatu Temple

One of Bali's most iconic cliffside temples, known for dramatic ocean views and traditional Kecak dance performances.

Padang Padang Beach

A popular destination for swimming, surfing, and coastal sightseeing.

Suluban Beach

Often referred to as Blue Point Beach, Suluban is famous for its unique limestone formations and surf culture.

Bingin Beach

A favourite destination among surfers and beach lovers seeking a relaxed atmosphere.

Meet and Greet at Bali Airport

Upon arrival at Ngurah Rai Airport, your driver will meet you after baggage collection.

The driver will assist with luggage and escort you to your vehicle before beginning the journey to Uluwatu.

This service is particularly useful for:

First-time visitors to Bali
Families travelling with children
Groups with multiple bags
Travellers carrying surfboards
Late-night arrivals
Frequently Asked Questions
How far is Uluwatu from Bali Airport?

Uluwatu is approximately 18 to 25 kilometres from Ngurah Rai Airport depending on the exact destination.

How long does it take to get from Bali Airport to Uluwatu?

The journey usually takes between 35 and 70 minutes depending on traffic conditions and destination.

What is the best way to get from Bali Airport to Uluwatu?

Many visitors choose private airport transfers because they offer fixed pricing, airport pickup, luggage assistance, and direct hotel drop-off.

Do you provide transfers to Bingin and Padang Padang?

Yes. Airport transfers are available throughout Uluwatu including Bingin, Padang Padang, Suluban, Pecatu, and Balangan.

Can I book an airport transfer before arriving in Bali?

Yes. Advance bookings are recommended, especially during peak holiday periods.

Do you provide airport transfers for surf travellers?

Yes. Airport transfers can accommodate travellers carrying surfboards and additional luggage, subject to vehicle selection.

